urses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(12,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 4 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 4 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-U-00150-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(13,'Outline','In addition to traditional issues faced by a business owner regarding the operation of his or her business, business ownership creates complexities in the tax, estate, and financial planning arenas. By focusing on the development of many unique business planning tools, this course explores the entrance and exit strategies available to business owners.At the end of this course you will be able to - Compare several options in the strategic area of buying, selling, and gifting business interests.Reasons to value a businessValuation methodsProfessional’s role in business valuationsSkill sets necessaryUnderstanding standards of valueUnderstanding levels of valueUnderstanding business valuation approaches',NULL,'Outline'),(14,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(15,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learne