do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(56,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 3 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 3 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00131-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(57,'Outline','Tax compliance issues for fiduciary entities are sometimes confusing to practitioners due to the fact that many lack experience in this area. This course (the first part of a two-part series) provides the practitioner with a practical understanding of the basic issues of estates and trusts. This knowledge will allow the practitioner to understand the basics of entities and the basics of Subchapter J of the Internal Revenue Code. Understanding these areas will allow the practitioner to start their understanding of tax compliance in preparing the U.S. Income Tax Return for Estates and Trusts (Form 1041).Specific issues regarding a decedent’s estateSpecific issues regarding a trustClassification of trust entitiesUnderstanding various fiduciary issuesUnderstanding the basics of Subchapter J of the Internal Revenue CodeIncome issuesDeduction issuesPass-through issues',NULL,'Outline'),(58,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(59,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(60,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 3 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 3 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00148-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(61,'Outline','In addition to tax compliance services, you as a tax professional are tasked with the responsibility to advise clients on potential changes in tax law that could create adverse consequences for your clients. 2020 was an exceptional year when it came to stimulus legislation. This legislation was paid for with “borrowed funds” that need to “paid back”. President Biden as well as other politicians have proposed significant changes to the Internal Revenue Code in the areas of individual income taxation, business income taxation, and estate and gift taxation.Although no actual legislation has been passed to date, changes are on the horizon. In order to better serve your clients, you must be knowledgeable of all potential changes so that you can create proper tax strategies for your clients. This course will give you the knowledge needed so that you can put your clients in the right direction. Focus will be put on the creation of coordinated financial, tax, and estate planning that will allow you to suggest integrated planning ideas for your clients.Explanation of “Integrated Tax, Financial, and Estate Planning”An understanding of President Joe Biden’s tax policies, ideas, and proposalsAn understanding of potential tax policies, ideas, and proposals of other politiciansPotential legislative changes in individual income taxationPotential legislative changes in business income taxationPotential legislative changes in estate and gift taxationPotential changes in long-term capital gain and qualified dividend ratesPotential return of the “Pease Limitation”How certain clients will need to deal with the potential for higher tax bracketsRetirement planning considerationsIncome and deduction planning ideasPotential Estate and Gift Tax changes and how to update a client’s planning needsPotential elimination of IRC §1014 (“Unlimited Step-up in Basis”)Potential elimination or modification of GRATsCharitable transaction planningQualified Opportunity Zone planningPotential changes in IRC §199A and how these changes might affect certain clientsRoth conversion ideasManaging business losses under harsh new loss limitation proposals',NULL,'Outline'),(62,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(63,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(64,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00127-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(65,'Outline','Employment tax returns have been pummeled by a flood of Congressional pandemic relief over and over and over again. Dripping with change after change after change, how do we push through and go on? This course will wash you employment tax clean.First, it was deferral of employer OASDI until 2021 and 2022. Next, sick pay and family leave to employees under FFCRA offset by all fed employment taxes (ET). PPP then blitzed America with intricate employment tax interplay. Then, the President allowed deferral of employee OASDI. Next, the employee retention credit (ERC) burst on the scene to retroactively co-exist alongside PPP loans and forgiveness, but not on the same wages. Next, Congress changed the ERC/ET interplay prospectively. After all of that, IRS weighed in (well, sort of).How do all of the above compete for the same wages and soak against the other?Amended return mania can put serious cash right back into your pocketHow Form 941 and 941-X doubled overnight in size and scopeEmployee retention credit (ERC) – The ET credit masquerading as a tax creditPlanning cash flow involving employment tax deposits and refundsExamples of various scenarios, filled out forms and backup recordsERC and FFCRA (and veteran’s employment, WOTC, R&D and §45S) credits and PPP forgiveness wage absorption all on displayDo it yourself or manage the outside payroll vendor? (How to prevent being slain)How ERC employment tax credits interact with income tax returns (let the M-1 adjustment good times roll)Planning, planning and planning to get every dollar you can get',NULL,'Outline'),(66,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(67,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished,