 enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(68,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00134-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(69,'Outline','United States taxpayers are required to report their worldwide income, including foreign income. In addition, in certain circumstances United States taxpayers must report foreign asset holdings, whether or not income was earned. We will discuss the requirements for reporting worldwide income from all sources including foreign accounts, paying taxes on the income from those accounts, and paying penalties for noncompliance.We will discuss FBAR reporting and penalties, types of foreign assets, comparison of Form 8938 and FBAR, passive foreign investment companies, the Offshore Voluntary Disclosure Initiative, and much more.During the class you will also learn the best methods for correcting prior failures to file required returns, and we will address when to file certain foreign informational returns. Specifically, you will learn the following:Learning ObjectivesWhen to file FinCEN Form 114Understanding the penalties and consequences for willful failure to file an FBARWhich assets are reportable on Form 8938 and the FBARThe filing threshold for gifts from foreign corporations or partnershipsThe standards for admission to the streamlined Offshore Voluntary Disclosure ProgramCourse OutlineForeign bank accountsForeign trustsForeign corporationsForeign partnerships',NULL,'Outline'),(70,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheim