ogin page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(88,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00114-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(89,'Outline','The Internal Revenue Service has revised its system of offers in compromise. Those changes have increased the probability of a successful offer in compromise. Practitioners must comply complex rules for settlement of outstanding tax obligations but with an understanding of the new rules you can substantially reduce many tax obligations. COVID-19 initiatives and proceduresTechniques for Valuing AssetsMaximizing IRS Allowable Expense StandardsEffective Tax Administration OffersReducing Hassles From Campus OIC FunctionariesAlternatives to Avoid the 20% Down paymentCase Studies and Live Q&A session',NULL,'Outline'),(90,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of