undation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(187,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(188,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 4 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 4 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00161-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(189,'Outline','The Times They Are a Changin’. Tax rates appear to be on the most certain long-term increase. Tax planning’s main objective is keeping tax rates at their lowest possible level through time. The time to capture low tax rates is exactly right now. Today, there’s an open window to optimally convert from a traditional IRA to a Roth – and it’s closing very soon. In this course, you’ll learn exactly how to prevent increasing tax rates (and other proposed changes) from seriously battering the value of a retirement nest egg.A Roth conversion is an intensely personal decision that requires impeccable attention to a client’s specifics. We’ll establish for you the Roth conversion thinking process and all things to consider.Why are Roth conversions screaming hot? Huge tax rate changes on the horizonImpact of (likely to pass) proposed legislation on IRAsExploring how the SECURE Act’s 10 year rule decimates most estate plansMost IRA trusts don’t work anymore – Roths to the rescueAdvantages of any IRA owner converting – Regardless of income tax bracketThe Roth conversion evaluation processBenefits and pitfalls of a Roth conversionProjecting income tax on conversions – The many impacts of the gameExtraordinary Roth IRA estate planning/estate tax advantages now and laterThe beauty of no income tax at retirement (will I run out of money?)How to avoid paying too much tax on a Roth conversionThe permanent nature of a Roth conversion (the hard TCJA hand slap)IRA conversion myths to promptly dispose ofKnow that you know when to (or not) move your checker on the board',NULL,'Outline'),(190,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(191,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recordi