 will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(192,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 3 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet Based NASBA and IRS Credits: 3 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00156-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(193,'Outline','Are you interested in how cryptocurrencies were developed and how they work? Does blockchain technology provide sufficient security for cryptocurrencies? What are the advantages and disadvantages of using cryptocurrencies? What are the tax consequences of investing in cryptocurrencies or using them for personal or business transactions? This course is designed for individuals who would like to obtain a basic understanding of crypto currency.The course will cover the history of virtual currencies and explain how they work. We will review some of the legal issues involved with virtual currencies. The course will cover the advantages and disadvantages of using virtual currencies. We will review the IRS rules for tracking and reporting crypto currency transactions for tax purposes.Define cryptocurrencyRecognize the tax implications of using or investing in cryptocurrencyIdentify how the IRS defines virtual currencyIdentify advantages and disadvantages to using cryptocurrencyDescribe the first cyptopcurrency and when it was created and releasedDifferentiate correct statements regarding the history of BitcoinRecognize case studies and how they could apply to your clientsDifferentiate correct statements with respect to virtual currencies and taxesIdentify most commonly used currencies',NULL,'Outline'),(194,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as hig