respondence audits. This class will cover the minority of audits where the IRS personally contacts the taxpayer and ask to conduct an exam at her home or business.When a taxpayer is in a cash-intensive business the IRS uses special techniques to find unreported income. A practitioner must know be cognizant of each of the methods the IRS uses to find a client’s unreported cash receipts.IRS audit selection techniquesThe use of Audit Technique Guides for cash-intensive businessesBank deposits methodCash disbursements methodCash T analysis',NULL,'Outline'),(298,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(299,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credit