ms logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(308,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00103-20-O',NULL,'Credits'),(309,'Outline','As Coronavirus wreaks economic havoc, Congress and IRS have acted swiftly through the tax law in response. These relief efforts cut much deeper and wider than first meet the eye. By now, we’re 3 rounds of legislation and many rounds of IRS (and Labor) guidance into this thing. Let us cut your learning curve.The Coronavirus has wreaked economic havoc and Congress, as well as the IRS, have needed to act swiftly with regards to tax laws. As of March 28, 2020, President Donald Trump signed the CARES (Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security) Act. This course will discuss the tax and liquidity planning in response to the CARES Act. The IRS has postponed some deadlines, but not all. You will be equipped with navigating the many questions surrounding the deferral of 2019 tax payments. Additionally, a Families First Act has been signed, providing a stimulus package for those affected financially by the Covid-19 pandemic. This course will detail the IRS’s rapidly changing approach to collections, statute of limitation protections, and operations. By the end of this course, you will know how these new and sudden changes affect your clients and enable you to answer the many questions they may have as a result of these changes.Because the details surrounding the Coronavirus are uncertain, the legislation is ever-changing. The information in this course is intended to provide information on new legislation that has been put in place up until this point. As any potential major changes occur, those who take this program will be kept up to date.Objectives:At the end of this course, you will be able to:Explain the Stafford Act Emergency DeclarationInterpret the Families First Coronavirus Response ActDiscuss the CARES ActDiscuss and interpret details surrounding the Tax Payment and Tax Filing ReliefsHighlights:Stafford Act Emergency DeclarationIRS Notice 2020-17 – Tax Payment ReliefIRS Notice 2020-18 – Tax Filing ReliefFiling and Payment Deadline IRS FAQFamilies First Coronavirus Response ActCARES Act ',NULL,'Outline'),(310,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(311,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and