 you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(368,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 1 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 1 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID:QQTMI-T-00065-20-O',NULL,'Credits'),(369,'Outline','Participants will receive knowledge of the remedies available for resolving penalties and interest. The event will provide practical tips, procedures and forms for requesting penalty relief (both First Time Abatement and Reasonable Cause). This is a replay of the event which was aired on 19th July 2019The objective of this lecture is to provide an overview of certain penalties, including accuracy-related penalties, fraud penalties, understatement of valuations, reporting requirement penalties, failure to file, failure to pay, and failure to deposit and the circumstances under which penalties and interest can be abated.  The presentation will focus on the IRS factors for Reasonable Cause abatement and the circumstances under which interest on the taxes can be waived.  Participants will learn the forms and procedures used for requesting penalty and interest abatement (including the First Time Abatement for penalties).Learn the rules on waiver of penalties and interestReview forms and procedures for requesting reliefWhat are the requirements and procedures for First Time Abatement What are the factors for Reasonable Cause abatementLearn the procedures for requesting refund of paid penaltiesPractical Tips from the Trenches on Requesting Relief for Penalties and Interest',NULL,'Outline'),(370,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Al