ll be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(396,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00055-20-O',NULL,'Credits'),(397,'Outline','On July 1 , 2019 - President Trump signed the new Taxpayer First Act (TFA) into law. TFA provides the first significant taxpayer rights enhancement since 1998. The Act is designed to strengthen taxpayer rights, particularly with appeals, enhance customer service (long-term), improve information technology and cybersecurity, protect and encourage more whistle-blowing, and improve overall efficiency and effectiveness of the IRS. The IRS Appeals Officer will be more independent and seizures of assets will be more restricted. Attorney Robert E. McKenzie will discuss the provisions of the new law in detail.Establish the IRS Independent Office of Appeals to resolve federal tax controversies without litigation;Require the IRS to develop a comprehensive customer service strategy;Exempt certain low-income taxpayers from payments required to submit an offer-in-compromise;Modify tax enforcement procedures that address issues such as the seizure of property, issuing a summons, joint liability, referral for private debt collection, and contacting third parties;Establish requirements for responding to Taxpayer Advocate Directives;Modify procedures for whistle-blowers;Establish requirements for cybersecurity and identify protection;Prohibit the rehiring of certain IRS employees who were removed for misconduct;Allow the IRS to require additional taxpayers to file returns electronically; andIncrease the penalty for failing to file a return.Gain valuable knowledge that will allow you to protect your clients rights.',NULL,'Outline'),(398,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(399,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If 