gistration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(408,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 Hours Session Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: BasicDelivery method: Group Internet Based NASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-U-00024-19-O',NULL,'Credits'),(409,'Outline','This webinar will discuss the implications of the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act of 2017 (TCJA) on the real estate and construction industry. We will review key provisions of TCJA including accounting methods, depreciation, carried interest, the limitation on business interest deductions, net operating loss limitations, and the 20% qualified business income deduction as they impact developers, investors and contractors’ decisions moving forward in 2018 and onward.The webinar will specifically focus on the alternative depreciation schedules, the holding period for section 1231 gains and 1250 depreciation recapture, and the section 1031 like-kind exchange rules for businesses in the real estate industry such as hotels, skilled nursing facilities, assisted living facilities that are comprised of real estate and personal property assets.Examine key provisions in TCJA that impact businesses operating in the real estate and construction industry.Provide examples of how businesses can mitigate the negative impact of certain TCJA provisions through planning strategies.Consider the choice of entity considerations and the projected financial benefits of converting existing entities to optimize after-tax returns.Planning opportunities and choice of entity considerations for businesses operating in the real estate and construction industry.',NULL,'Outline'),(410,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(411,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For g