 the practitioner to make a well-informed decision as to whether or not a trust is the appropriate vehicle for a client’s financial, estate, and/or asset protection plan, and, if so, how the trust can best be implemented and operated.The objective of this lecture is to provide a practical understanding of when and how to implement and operate a trust in a client’s financial, estate, and/or asset protection plan. Participants will learn about the many different types of trusts that can be harnessed to save clients income, estate, generation-skipping, and other taxes, at both the federal and state level. The role of the trustee and how to avoid problemsHow to use trusts to avoid probateHow revocable living trusts are affected by income, gift, and estate taxesHow an irrevocable trust can be the center of an estate planDynasty trust issuesTrust options to provide security for older clientsCharitable trust issuesHow trusts can serve as asset protection devices',NULL,'Outline'),(478,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(479,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. 