ASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00148-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(513,'Outline','In this two-hour program Attorney Eric Green will explain the ins and outs of helping the struggling business resolve its outstanding payroll tax issue, and how to handle the potential personal liability by owners and employees. Most small businesses end up dealing with the IRS Collection Division due to payroll tax issues. Eric will discuss third party liability, and strategies for minimizing or avoiding personal liability. Finally, eric will explain the various options available to resolve the issue for the business and owners/employees.  Describe and outline the steps to resolving payroll liabilities Identify the trust tax concepts of personal liability for responsible parties  Recognize and apply a strategy for getting a payroll tax client current and compliant  Identify the penalty for failure to deposit if the deposit is not made within 10 days after the first delinquency noticeDifferentiate statements with respect to payroll taxes Describe trust funds  Recognize types of responsibility alone is insufficient to establish responsible person statusDifferentiate court cases and how they apply to clients Describe employment tax prosecutionsIdentify how to determine who is responsible Differentiate IRC Sections',NULL,'Outline'),(514,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation o