: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00198-22-O',NULL,'Credits'),(525,'Outline','This live presentation covers the TOP TEN things every accountant should know, in the back of her mind, about tax problem and how they may be resolved. Then, they’ll recognize issues for their client and be able to direct them in the right direction!Most accountants have a basic understanding about IRS letters, audits, small collection matters. But shouldn’t you know a little something about statutes of limitations? How to handle the receipt of a Notice of Deficiency? When you should not file a joint return?When to make monthly estimated tax paymentsShould you extend the ASED (Audit Statute of Limitations)How to handle the receipt of a 90-day letter (and avoiding malpractice!)Analyzing proposed audit adjustmentsWhen to file tax returns “married filing separate” to avoid malpracticeBrief explanation of how to calculate an Offer in CompromiseStatutes of LimitationsBrief explanation of Trust Fund Recovery Penalty (and avoiding malpractice)When income taxes can be discharged through bankruptcy',NULL,'Outline'),(526,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.a