ertain long-term increase. Tax planning’s main objective is keeping tax rates at their lowest possible level through time. The time to capture low tax rates is exactly right now. Today, there’s an open window to optimally convert from a traditional IRA to a Roth – and it’s closing very soon. In this course, you’ll learn exactly how to prevent increasing tax rates (and other proposed changes) from seriously battering the value of a retirement nest egg.A Roth conversion is an intensely personal decision that requires impeccable attention to a client’s specifics. We’ll establish for you the Roth conversion thinking process and all things to consider.Why are Roth conversions screaming hot? Huge tax rate changes on the horizonImpact of (likely to pass) proposed legislation on IRAsExploring how the SECURE Act’s 10 year rule decimates most estate plansMost IRA trusts don’t work anymore – Roths to the rescueAdvantages of any IRA owner converting – Regardless of income tax bracketThe Roth conversion evaluation processBenefits and pitfalls of a Roth conversionProjecting income tax on conversions – The many impacts of the gameExtraordinary Roth IRA estate planning/estate tax advantages now and laterThe beauty of no income tax at retirement (will I run out of money?)How to avoid paying too much tax on a Roth conversionThe permanent nature of a Roth conversion (the hard TCJA hand slap)IRA conversion myths to promptly dispose ofKnow that you know when to (or not) move your checker on the board',NULL,'Outline'),(558,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, ap