fore the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(564,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet Based NASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00199-22-O',NULL,'Credits'),(565,'Outline','This course helps the practitioner understand not only how to make the portability election, but how it can provide overall tax benefits to surviving spouses and beneficiary of estates that fall below the federal estate exclusion amount. We will look at who should and can make the election, how the election is made and how to opt out, the requirements for filing Form 706, along with comparing the benefits of electing portability to conventional credit shelter trust planning.ObjectiveTo provide the practitioner with the knowledge to help their client decide whether to make the portability election and the mechanics and process of filing form 706 to elect or out-out of electing portability.Course OutlineDefining portability, a.k.a. the deceased spousal unused exemption (DSUE) electionHow to calculate the DSUE amountMaking the portability electionWho can and cannot elect portabilityReview the requirements for completing form 706 when electing portabilityMaking a late election and IRS Section 9100 reliefHow to opt-out of the election and hazards of not making the election for the client and practitionerDetermining the “last deceased spouse” for making the electionIRS examination issues when making the electionReview benefits and drawbacks of the DSUE election vs. conventional credit shelter/asset protection planning - income taxes vs. estate taxesUse of QTIPs and QDOTsA look at state death tax issues',NULL,'Outline'),(566,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information vis