ferred revenueTreatment of transaction costsBasics of mixed entity transactions, examples such as:C-Corp buys an interest in a partnershipC-Corp buys an S-CorpC-Corp buys an interest in an LLC (lots of possibilities here)S-Corp buys a partnershipS-Corp buys a C-CorpS-Corp buys an interest in an LLCPartnership acquisitions of various entity typesVery basic overview of tax-free re-organizationsHigh level overview of entity formationsHigh level of entity liquidations or terminations',NULL,'Outline'),(606,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(607,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to en