bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(616,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00176-22-O',NULL,'Credits'),(617,'Outline','On IRS 2021 Forms 1065, Schedules K-1 and Instructions, IRS continues to ask for tons of detailed information and they’ve changed up the way they ask for it. In a jolting new move, IRS has made every domestic U.S. Form 1065 preparer responsible to prepare and file Schedules K-2 and K-3 (re: international) (though 99% of the time not relevant) or else do massive new due diligence to sidestep it. This course shows you exactly what to do in response.In a huge new development, IRS released Rev. Procs. 2021-48, -49 and -50 to allow taxpayers the choice to report PPP debt relief income (and, thus, deduct PPP funded expenses) in their tax year of choice. This opens up a tax planning extravaganza.Course OutlineHow new Schedules K-2 and K-3 knock Form 1065 out of orbit (until mid-March of 2022) and impose stunning new duties on a 1065 preparer’s shouldersTweaked (once again) tax basis capital account reporting – What must be computed and disclosed (and by when)Extraordinary new available tax planning: How partnerships (and S Corps) enjoy optional new timing choices for placement of PPP debt relief incomePlethora of other new info required (built-in gains lying in wait, disregarded entity partners, new tiered partnership reporting and more)Learning ObjectivesCapital accounts – Tax basis reporting tweaked again2021 Form 1065 and Schedule K-1 – Reporting requirements in depthDisregarded entity partners – Disclosures, depth of implications3 year average annual gross receipts test – 5 places it mattersBasis in partner’s partnership interest – New timing, timing, timing, timingDisguised sales – Form 1065 question re: partner disclosure§704(c) Built-in gains and loss – New “as-you-go” info requiredAggregation of at-risk activities – Disclosures with sticky implicationsGrouping of passive activities – Disclosure and detail requiredHow every domestic (and foreign) partnership must immediately concern itself with all-new Schedules K-2 and K-3',NULL,'Outline'),(618,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(619,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(620,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 3 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 3 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID:QQTMI-T-00171-22-O',NULL,'Credits'),(621,'Outline','In the foreign information reporting context, arguably no form creates as much consternation in the context of penalty exposure as the Foreign Bank Account Report (better known as the FBAR). Statutorily, willful failures to file FBARs create massive penalty exposure: the greater of $100,000 or 50% of the balance of unreported accounts for the year in question (with a six-year civil statute of limitations). In the FBAR penalty context, the primary focus is typically given to the interpretation of the willful standard - and how it connects to maximum penalty exposure.This course will focus on FBAR requirements while also providing an overview of other information reporting requirements relevant for multinational taxpayers.Cover general reporting requirements for FBAR purposes – who is required to file, reportable accounts, etc.Penalties assessable for FBAR failures – non willful and willful penalties, and the standards for imposition of the sameEnforcement of FBAR penaltiesTitle 26 forms required – Form 5471, Form 3520, Form 8938, Form 8621, Form 8865Retroactive Disclosure OptionsFBAR Cases and examples',NULL,'Outline'),(622,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(623,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not s