rm.Review of Entities and Subchapter J IssuesHow to prepare a Form 1041Understanding of distributable net income (DNI)Understanding of income in respect of a decedent (IRD)Line-by-line instruction (Income, Deductions, and Payments)Schedule A (Charitable Deduction)Schedule B (Income Distribution Deduction)Other schedulesProper compliance regarding “Other Information”',NULL,'Outline'),(654,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(655,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(656,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 4 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 4 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00161-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(657,'Outline','On recent IRS Forms 1065, Schedules K-1 and in related instructions, IRS launches massive reporting requirements re: negative tax basis capital accounts, at-risk activities, passive activities, partner level built-in gains, disregarded entities and many more. Chaos has resulted.We can’t wait to be a deer in the headlights preparing Form 1065 and Schedules K-1. In this action packed program, you’ll learn: Negative tax basis capital account reporting – What must be computed and disclosed (and by when) – How IRS keeps moving the targetHow partnerships (and S Corps) face the at-risk (and passive) activity reporting blues (and what to do about them)Plethora of other new info required re: built-in gains lying in waitConsequence laden all new reporting re: disregarded entity partnersNew disguised sale reportingNew disclosures re: liabilities of partnerStunning penalties for failure to wholly and accurately complete K-1',NULL,'Outline'),(658,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(659,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners 