r query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(672,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 4 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: Three to four years’ experience with mergers and acquisitionsSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 4 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00179-22-O',NULL,'Credits'),(673,'Outline','It appears that there will be a multitude of tax law changes in 2021. Practitioners need to be aware of any potential changes so that they may advise their clients accordingly, especially in the area of qualified plans and IRAs. Now is the time to contemplate potential changes as well as develop strategies so that your client can successfully deal with these potential changes in the law. This course provides the practitioner with ideas to help a client “roll with the punches”!Learning ObjectiveAt the end of this course, the participant will be able to both understand potential tax law changes and be able to assist a client in creating successful strategies to deal with such potential changes in the qualified plan and IRA arenas.Course OutlineRoth conversion strategies – When and how muchUnderstanding the changes made by the SECURE Act corelate with changes in the tax lawUsing trusts as a beneficiary of an IRARollover strategiesFederal Estate Tax issues in a changing tax environmentPost-Mortem opportunitiesSpousal issues (including QTIP issues)Proper beneficiary planning ideas',NULL,'Outline'),(674,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(675,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(676,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: Basic understanding of taxation, financial planning, and estate planningSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet Based NASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00121-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(677,'Outline','Participants will receive knowledge of the remedies available for resolving penalties and interest. The event will provide practical tips, procedures and forms for requesting penalty relief (both First Time Abatement and Reasonable Cause). This is a replay of the event which was aired on 19th July 2019The objective of this lecture is to provide an overview of certain penalties, including accuracy-related penalties, fraud penalties, understatement of valuations, reporting requirement penalties, failure to file, failure to pay, and failure to deposit and the circumstances under which penalties and interest can be abated.  The presentation will focus on the IRS factors for Reasonable Cause abatement and the circumstances under which interest on the taxes can be waived.  Participants will learn the forms and procedures used for requesting penalty and interest abatement (including the First Time Abatement for penalties).Learn the rules on waiver of penalties and interestReview forms and procedures for requesting reliefWhat are the requirements and procedures for First Time Abatement What are the factors for Reasonable Cause abatementLearn the procedures for requesting refund of paid penaltiesPractical Tips from the Trenches on Requesting Relief for Penalties and Interest',NULL,'Outline'),(678,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(679,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(680,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet Based NASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-U-00031-19-O',NULL,'Credits'),(681,'Outline','As Coronavirus wreaks economic havoc, Congress and IRS have acted swiftly through the tax law in response. These relief efforts cut much deeper and wider than first meet the eye. By now, we’re 3 rounds of legislation and many rounds of IRS (and Labor) guidance into this thing. Let us cut your learning curve.The Coronavirus has wreaked economic havoc and Congress, as well as the IRS, have needed to act swiftly with regards to tax laws. As of March 28, 2020, President Donald Trump signed the CARES (Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security) Act. This course will discuss the tax and liquidity planning in response to the CARES Act. The IRS has postponed some deadlines, but not all. You will be equipped with navigating the many questions surrounding the deferral of 2019 tax payments. Additionally, a Families First Act has been signed, providing a stimulus package for those affected financially by the Covid-19 pandemic. This course will detail the IRS’s rapidly changing approach to collections, statute of limitation protections, and operations. By the end of this course, you will know how these new and sudden changes affect your clients and enable you to answer the many questions they may have as a result of these changes.Because the details surrounding the Coronavirus are uncertain, the legislation is ever-changing. The information in this course is intended to provide information on new legislation that has been put in place up until this point. As any potential major changes occur, those who take this program will be kept up to date.Objectives:At the end of this course, you will be able to:Explain the Stafford Act Emergency DeclarationInterpret the Families First Coronavirus Response ActDiscuss the CARES ActDiscuss and interpret details surrounding the Tax Payment and Tax Filing ReliefsHighlights:Stafford Act Emergency DeclarationIRS Notice 2020-17 – Tax Payment ReliefIRS Notice 2020-18 – Tax Filing ReliefFiling and Payment Deadline IRS FAQFamilies First Coronavirus Response ActCARES Act ',NULL,'Outline'),(682,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(683,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has 