ack experience in this area. This course (the first part of a two-part series) provides the practitioner with a practical understanding of the basic issues of estates and trusts. This knowledge will allow the practitioner to understand the basics of entities and the basics of Subchapter J of the Internal Revenue Code. Understanding these areas will allow the practitioner to start their understanding of tax compliance in preparing the U.S. Income Tax Return for Estates and Trusts (Form 1041).Specific issues regarding a decedent’s estateSpecific issues regarding a trustClassification of trust entitiesUnderstanding various fiduciary issuesUnderstanding the basics of Subchapter J of the Internal Revenue CodeIncome issuesDeduction issuesPass-through issues',NULL,'Outline'),(726,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(727,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and n