d party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(728,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 3 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 3 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-T-00148-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(729,'Outline','In 2021, the IRS has promised more aggressive action to collect the billions in unpaid taxes that have already been assessed and are on the books. An area of consistent focus is nominee and alter ego claims, and fraudulent conveyances which it frequently pursues as an easy target.Become familiar with what the IRS looks for in a “fraudulent conveyance”Counsel your client appropriately in connection with asset transfersUnderstand the difference between nominee liens and alter ego liensWhat is a nominee lienWhat is an alter-ego lienLearn your defenses and options to challenge these claims by IRS',NULL,'Outline'),(730,'GiveAway','We donate $1 to the Alzheimers Foundation of America every time you buy a course from us.Alzheimers Disease is the 6th leading cause of death in the United States.In 2019, Alzheimers and other dementias will cost the nation $290 billion. By 2050 these costs could rise as high as $1.1 trillion.5.8 million Americans are living with Alzheimers. This number is projected to grow to nearly 14 million by 2050.We dont want to sit around doing nothing. Therefore, apart from serving our customers, we want to be a part of the next breakthrough in Alzheimers treatment.CPE Warehouse donates $1 of every purchase you make to the Alzheimers Foundation of America.(For more information visit www.alzfdn.org/)',NULL,'GivingBack'),(731,'FAQ','I can’t find my CPE Certificate. What should I do?Every learner has access to their learners portal, via our website, where certificates are kept for ease of access. Please log into the learners portal with the details that were provided to you upon registration. If you are not able to find your login details, you can reset your password. We also email certificates to all learners after each course. Check your inbox (incl. spam folder). If something seems amiss, and neither options are available, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comI couldn’t attend, can you send me the recording?24 hours after an event has finished, all learners receive a copy of the recording (without CPE Credits). Please check your inbox (and your spam folders) to ensure that you have received the recording.Can I mail you a cheque as payment?For group orders we do allow cheque orders as long as we are set up as a preferred vendor with your organization. We only accept cheques for orders valued over $1000.I need a refund. What are my options?We offer refunds under the following circumstances:Cancelling attendance 24 hours before the event.Not satisfied with our event/recording: If you are not happy with our event we will gladly issue a refund. All we ask is that you provide us with detailed feedback. We know we are not perfect!If your situation does not fall in the above two options, email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com or contact us via the chat bot on our website to further discuss your situation with us.My discount code didn’t work!Make sure that there are no spaces between the letters and numbers, and that your discount code does not have an expiration date.Still have issues? We have a handy chat bot on our website that can help you with this during office hours. If you require assistance outside of office hours, you can email your query to cpe@cpewarehouse.comI can’t attend the event – How do I cancel my registration?Cancellations are available within 24 hours before an event begins. After this point, cancellation is no longer possible. Just email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.com and we will take it from there.I don’t remember my password!Please request a password re-set via our website, on the login page. Should you still have problems logging in, please email us at cpe@cpewarehouse.comDoes this course count towards CLE?Unfortunately, our courses do not provide CLE credits…yet!Do you sell through other websites?We currently do not sell our courses on other third party platforms. However, we are always looking to provide our courses to our students and therefore partnerships will be announced to all learners as we enter into these.',NULL,'Other'),(732,'Credit & Other Info','Session Duration: 2 HoursSession Prerequisites and preparation: NoneSession learning level: IntroductoryDelivery method: Group Internet BasedNASBA and IRS Credits: 2 Tax HoursIRS CE Provider #: QQTMINASBA Sponsor #: 143337IRS Course ID: QQTMI-U-00117-21-O',NULL,'Credits'),(733,'outline','afsaddsfsdfdsf',NULL,'Outline'),(734,'outline','asdf','asfaf','Outline'),(735,'outline',NULL,'dasdfdssafsdfsdfasfssdff','Outline'),(736,'Course Outline','<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><span style=\"font-family:\'JetBrains Mono\', monospace;\">This course covers the essentials of IRA’s.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>We’ll go well beyond the basics to cover crucial topics: when to convert traditional IRA’s to Roth IRA’s, how to minimize tax on conversion, and when clients should recharacterize IRA contributions (and how to recharacterize).&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Also discuss how to get a waiver for clients who fail to take a required minimum distributions and other traps in the IRA area including prohibited transactions, excess contributions, and impermissible investments.</p>','','Other'),(737,'Credits and Other Info','<p><strong>Session Duration:</strong>&nbsp;2 Hours</p>\n<p><strong>Session Prerequisites and preparation:</strong> <!--StartFragment-->None<!--EndFragment--><strong><br><br>Session learning level:</strong> Introductory<strong><br><br>Delivery method:</strong> Group Internet Based<strong><br><br>NASBA and IRS Credits:</strong>&nbsp;2 Tax Hours<strong><br><br>IRS CE Provider #:</strong> QQTMI<strong><br><br>NASBA Sponsor #:</strong> 143337<br><br><strong>IRS Course ID:&nbsp;</strong><!--StartFragment--><!--StartFragment--><!--StartFragment-->QQTMI-T-00141-21-O<!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p>',NULL,'Other'),(738,'Course Outline','<p><span class=\"text-big\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:Georgia, serif;\">The field of&nbsp;estate&nbsp;planning&nbsp;is increasingly complex. Finding appropriate solutions to a client’s&nbsp;estate&nbsp;issues upon his/her death are critical to many areas, including the&nbsp;estate&nbsp;tax return of the decedent, the decedent’s final income tax return, the income tax return of the&nbsp;estate&nbsp;of the decedent, and the&nbsp;estate&nbsp;and financial&nbsp;planning&nbsp;issues of the heirs of the decedent.&nbsp;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\"><strong><u>Course Outline1</u></strong></span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Alternative valuation date (AVD) issues</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Portability Issues</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Installment payments of estate taxes (IRC Section 6166)</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">QTIP elections under IRC §2056(b)(7)</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">The use of qualified disclaimers</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Basis issues</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Issues involving the payment of estimated taxes</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Final income tax return of the decedent</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Medical expenses of final illness</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Savings bond interest acceleration</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Estate fiscal year and accounting method elections</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Passing out administrative expenses to maximize benefits to beneficiaries</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">The sixty-five-day rule election</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Income and deductions in respect of the decedent (IRD)</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Georgia, serif;\">Issues involving qualified plans and IRAs</span><br>&nbsp;</p>','','Other'),(739,'Course Outline','<p>Testb bdsafsdf sdfdsfsdfsdfds</p>','<p>sdf</p>','Other'),(740,'Outlines','<p>sdffsdfsdfsf</p>','','Outline'),(741,'Course Outline','<p>Test</p>','','Other'),(742,'Course Outline','<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\">This course will provide an overview of many of the tax issues Canadians and their advisors must address before, during and after the person becomes a U.S. resident.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\"><strong><u>Course Outline</u></strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Issues to be addressed before moving to the U.S.</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">First year in the U.S.</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Overview of the Canada-US Tax Treaty</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Canadian taxation of nonresidents</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Canadian Retirement Plans, Pensions and Social Security</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">U.S. Estate and Gift Tax</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Leaving the U.S.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\"><strong><u>Learning Objectives</u></strong></span><br><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\">At the end of this course you will be able to:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Identify issues that should be addressed before moving to the U.S.</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Recognize and make appropriate first year income tax elections</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Have a basic understanding of the Canada-US Tax Treaty</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Understand how Canada taxes its nonresidents</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Have a basic understanding of Canadian Retirement Plans, Pensions and Social Security and how they should be reported for U.S. tax purposes</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Overview of nonresident and non-U.S. &nbsp;Citizen Estate Tax</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Understand the issues involved of Green Card holders and U.S. citizens leaving the U.S., whether they keep or give up their status as Permanent Residents or Citizens</span></li></ul>','','Other'),(743,'Credits and Other Info','<p><strong>Session Duration:</strong>&nbsp;2 Hours</p><p><strong>Session Prerequisites and preparation:</strong> None<br><br><strong>Session learning level:</strong> Introductory<br><br><strong>Delivery method:</strong> Group Internet Based<br><br><strong>NASBA and IRS Credits:</strong>&nbsp;2 Tax Hours<br><br><strong>IRS CE Provider #:</strong> QQTMI<br><br><strong>NASBA Sponsor #:</strong> 143337<br><br><strong>IRS Course ID:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\">QQTMI-T-00215-22-O</span></p>','','Other'),(744,'Course Outline','<p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\">This course will provide an overview of many of the tax issues Canadians and their advisors must address before, during and after the person becomes a U.S. resident.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\"><strong><u>Course Outline</u></strong></span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Issues to be addressed before moving to the U.S.</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">First year in the U.S.</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Overview of the Canada-US Tax Treaty</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Canadian taxation of nonresidents</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Canadian Retirement Plans, Pensions and Social Security</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">U.S. Estate and Gift Tax</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Leaving the U.S.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\"><strong><u>Learning Objectives</u></strong></span><br><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\">At the end of this course you will be able to:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Identify issues that should be addressed before moving to the U.S.</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Recognize and make appropriate first year income tax elections</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Have a basic understanding of the Canada-US Tax Treaty</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Understand how Canada taxes its nonresidents</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Have a basic understanding of Canadian Retirement Plans, Pensions and Social Security and how they should be reported for U.S. tax purposes</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Overview of nonresident and non-U.S. &nbsp;Citizen Estate Tax</span></li><li><span style=\"color:rgb(32,18,77);\">Understand the issues involved of Green Card holders and U.S. citizens leaving the U.S., whether they keep or give up their status as Permanent Residents or Citizens</span></li></ul>','','Other'),(745,'Credits and Other Info','<p><strong>Session Duration:</strong>&nbsp;2 Hours</p><p><strong>Session Prerequisites and preparation:</strong> None<br><br><strong>Session learning level:</strong> Introductory<br><br><strong>Delivery method:</strong> Group Internet Based<br><br><strong>NASBA and IRS Credits:</strong>&nbsp;2 Tax Hours<br><br><strong>IRS CE Provider #:</strong> QQTMI<br><br><strong>NASBA Sponsor #:</strong> 143337<br><br><strong>IRS Course ID:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(32,18,77);\">QQTMI-T-00215-22-O</span></p>','','Other'),(746,'Course Outline','<p>We’ll cover a brand new “Practice Unit” released by the IRS in 2022. We’ll also cover new cases, changes in Form 1120S, and new administrative guidance.</p><p><br><strong><u>Course Outline</u></strong></p><p>• &nbsp; &nbsp;New cases addressing reasonable compensation for shareholders.&nbsp;<br>• &nbsp; &nbsp;Changes to Form 1120S Schedule K-1<br>• &nbsp; &nbsp;IRS Form 7203</p><p><strong><u>Learning Objectives</u></strong></p><p>• &nbsp; &nbsp;Determine proper reasonable compensation for shareholders.&nbsp;<br>• &nbsp; &nbsp;Identify circumstances where S corp status is inadvertently terminated (and how to fix inadvertent terminations retroactively).<br>• &nbsp; &nbsp;Learn rules for computing reasonable compensation for shareholders.</p>','','Other'),(747,'outline','<p>ouyline</p>','<p>aaasdfssdf</p>','Outline'),(748,'Give Away','<p>gasdffsdfsdsd</p>','','GivingBack'),(749,'COURSE OUTLINE','<p>COURSE OUTLINE</p>','<p>COURSE OUTLINE</p>','Outline'),(750,'COURSE OUTLINE','<p>course outline course outline course outline e outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline <strong>course outline </strong><i><strong>course outline <u>course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline&nbsp;</u></strong></i></p>','<p>course outline course outline course outline e outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline <strong>course outline </strong><i><strong>course outline <u>course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline course outline&nbsp;</u></strong></i></p>','Outline'),(751,'COURSE OUTLINE','<p>faqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaq<strong>faqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaq</strong><i><strong>faqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaqfaq</strong></i></p>','<p>title</p>','Outline'),(752,'Course Outline','<p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">This comprehensive course explores the latest developments and emerging trends in qualified plans and Individual Retirement Accounts (IRAs). Designed for professionals in the financial and retirement planning industry, this course provides an in-depth analysis of new issues, legislation, and strategies affecting qualified plans and IRAs.Course participants will delve into a wide range of topics, including, tax law changes, plan design considerations, distribution planning, and compliance requirements.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\"><strong>Course Outline</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp; * Legislative Updates: Explore the latest changes in laws and regulations governing qualified plans and IRAs, including all relevant parts of SECURE 2.0.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp; * Plan Design Considerations: Learn about innovative plan design strategies to enhance participant engagement, optimize tax advantages, and address evolving workforce demographics.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp; * Distribution Planning: Discover effective distribution strategies for retirement accounts, including required minimum distributions (RMDs), rollovers, and Roth conversions, with a focus on maximizing tax efficiency and meeting clients\' income needs.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp; * Client Engagement and Communication: Learn effective strategies for engaging clients in retirement planning discussions, communicating complex concepts, and providing personalized recommendations based on their unique needs and goals.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\"><strong>Learning Objective</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">At the end of this course, you will be able to:</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp;* &nbsp;Discuss the latest legislative and regulatory changes impacting qualified plans and IRAs</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp;* &nbsp;Identify the key differences between various types of qualified plans and IRAs and their suitability for different client scenarios.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp;* &nbsp;Identify plan design considerations to maximize tax advantages and employee participation.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp;* &nbsp;Discuss the impact of legislative changes on qualified plans and IRAs.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp;* &nbsp;Discuss emerging trends and innovative approaches in retirement planning, including Roth conversions, HSAs, and self-directed IRAs.</span><br><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">&nbsp;* &nbsp;Discuss practical skills in analyzing client needs, recommending suitable plans, and implementing effective retirement strategies.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">Live Q&amp;A session will be held after the event</span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\"><strong>Who Should Attend?</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">CPAs, EAs, attorneys, finance professionals, and financial planners</span></p>','','Other'),(753,'Credits and Other Info','<p><strong>Session Duration:</strong>&nbsp;2 Hours</p><p><strong>Session Prerequisites and preparation:</strong> <!--StartFragment-->None<!--EndFragment--><br><br><strong>Session learning level:</strong> Introductory<br><br><strong>Delivery method:</strong> Group Internet Based<br><br><strong>NASBA and IRS Credits:</strong>&nbsp;2 Tax Hours<br><br><strong>IRS CE Provider #:</strong> QQTMI<br><br><strong>NASBA Sponsor #:</strong> 143337<br><br><strong>IRS Course ID:&nbsp;</strong><!--StartFragment--><!--StartFragment--><!--StartFragment-->QQTMI-T-00141-21-O<!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p>','','Other'),(754,'Course Outline','<p><span style=\"font-family:Arial, \'Helvetica Neue\', Helvetica, \'Source Sans Pro\', sans-serif;\">This comprehensive course explores the latest developments and emerging trends in qualified plans and Individual Retirement Accounts (IRAs). Designed for professionals in the financial and retirement planning industry, this course provides an in-depth analysis of new issues, legislation, and strategies affecti